cite23†Gemini for Science†ai.google cite24†Experimental Tools†labs.google cite25†Science Skills†antigravity.google L84: \nL85: About\nL86: ## Our mission is to build AI responsibly to benefit humanity\nL87: \nL88: cite26†About Google DeepMind L89: \nL90: Learn more\nL91: \nL92: cite29†Education cite30†Our National Partnerships for AI cite31†Accelerator programs cite32†The Podcast cite33†DeepMind Institute†institute.deepmind.com L93: \nL94: cite15†Responsibility Ensuring AI safety through proactive security, even against evolving threats cite27†News Discover our latest AI breakthroughs, projects, and updates cite28†Careers We’re looking for people who want to make a real, positive impact on the world L95: cite34†Build with Gemini†aistudio.google.com cite35†Try Gemini†gemini.google.com L96: \nL97: cite36†Google DeepMind L98: \nL99: cite37†Google AI Learn about all our AI†ai.google cite38†Google DeepMind Explore the frontier of AI cite39†Google Labs Try our AI experiments†labs.google cite40†Google Research Explore our research†research.google L100: \nL101: Products and apps\nL102: cite35†Gemini app Chat with Gemini†gemini.google.com cite34†Google AI Studio Build with our next-gen AI models†aistudio.google.com cite41†Google Antigravity Our agentic development platform†antigravity.google L103: \nL104: cite0†Models L105: \nL106: cite10†Research L107: \nL108: cite17†Science L109: \nL110: cite26†About L111: \nL112: cite34†Build with Gemini†aistudio.google.com cite35†Try Gemini†gemini.google.com L113: \nL114: November 13, 2025 Research\nL115: # SIMA 2: An Agent that Plays, Reasons, and Learns With You in Virtual 3D Worlds\nL116: \nL117: SIMA Team\nL118: \nL119: cite42†Image: A four-column representation of SIMA 2, a Gemini-powered AI agent, acting within a 3D virtual environment.†lh3.googleusercontent.com L120: Last year, we cite43†introduced SIMA (Scalable Instructable Multiworld Agent), a generalist AI that could follow basic instructions across a wide range of virtual environments. SIMA was a crucial first step in teaching AI to translate language into meaningful action in rich, 3D worlds.\nL121: Today we’re introducing SIMA 2, the next milestone in our research creating general and helpful AI agents. By integrating the advanced capabilities of our cite1†Gemini models , SIMA is evolving from an instruction-follower into an interactive gaming companion. Not only can SIMA 2 follow human-language instructions in virtual worlds, it can now also think about its goals, converse with users, and improve itself over time.\nL122: This is a significant step in the direction of Artificial General Intelligence (AGI), with important implications for the future of robotics and AI-embodiment in general.\nL123: \nL124: cite44†SIMA 2: An agent that plays, reasons, and learns with you in virtual 3D worlds†www.youtube.com L125: \nL126:   * cite45†Reasoning L127:   * cite46†Generalization L128:   * cite47†Self-Improvement L129:   * cite48†Next steps L130:   * cite49†Responsibility L131: ## The Power of Reasoning\nL132: \nL133: The first version of SIMA learned to perform over 600 language-following skills, like “turn left,” “climb the ladder,” and “open the map,” across a diverse set of commercial video games. It operated in these environments as a person might, by “looking” at the screen and using a virtual keyboard and mouse to navigate, without access to the underlying game mechanics.\nL134: With SIMA 2, we’ve moved beyond instruction-following. By embedding a Gemini model as the agent's core, SIMA 2 can do more than just respond to instructions, it can think and reason about them.\nL135: \nL136: cite50†Image cite51†Image L137: \nL138: Your browser does not support the video tag. Your browser does not support the video tag.\nL139: \nL140: MineDojo: SIMA 1 (left) attempts to follow the instruction while SIMA 2 (right) successfully completes the task in a game it has never seen before.\nL141: \nL142: cite50†Image cite51†Image L143: Your browser does not support the video tag. Your browser does not support the video tag.\nL144: \nL145: ASKA: SIMA 1 (left) attempts to follow the instruction “Find a campfire” while SIMA 2 (right) successfully completes the task in a game it has never seen before.\nL146: \nL147: SIMA 2’s new architecture integrates Gemini’s powerful reasoning abilities to help it understand a user’s high-level goal, perform complex reasoning in pursuit, and skillfully execute goal-oriented actions within games.\nL148: We trained SIMA 2 using a mixture of human demonstration videos with language labels as well as Gemini-generated labels. As a result, SIMA 2 can now describe to the user what it intends to do and detail the steps it's taking to accomplish its goals.\nL149: \nL150: Slide 1 of 3\nL151: \nL152: cite50†Image cite51†Image L153: \nL154: Your browser does not support the video tag. Your browser does not support the video tag.\nL155: Moving beyond simple instruction following: SIMA 2 can answer the user’s questions and also reasons about its own behavior as well as its environment.\nL156: \nL157: cite50†Image cite51†Image L158: \nL159: Your browser does not support the video tag. Your browser does not support the video tag.\nL160: \nL161: Moving beyond simple instruction following: SIMA 2 can answer the user’s questions and also reasons about its own behavior as well as its environment.\nL162: \nL163: cite50†Image cite51†Image L164: Your browser does not support the video tag. Your browser does not support the video tag.\nL165: \nL166: Moving beyond simple instruction following: SIMA 2 can answer the user’s questions and also reasons about its own behavior as well as its environment.\nL167: \nL168: In testing, we have found that interacting with the agent feels less like giving it commands and more like collaborating with a companion who can reason about the task at hand.\nL169: And thanks to our collaboration with our existing and new game partners (see, Acknowledgements), we have been able to train and evaluate SIMA 2 on a wider array of games.\nL170: \nL171: This is the power of Gemini brought to embodied AI: a world-class reasoning engine that can now perceive, understand, and take action in complex, interactive 3D environments.\nL172: \nL173: Slide 1 of 4\nL174: \nL175: cite50†Image cite51†Image L176: \nL177: Your browser does not support the video tag. Your browser does not support the video tag.\nL178: SIMA 2 interprets abstract concepts and logical commands by reasoning about its environment and the user's intent.\nL179: \nL180: cite50†Image cite51†Image L181: \nL182: Your browser does not support the video tag. Your browser does not support the video tag.\nL183: \nL184: SIMA 2 interprets abstract concepts and logical commands by reasoning about its environment and the user's intent.\nL185: \nL186: cite50†Image cite51†Image L187: \nL188: Your browser does not support the video tag. Your browser does not support the video tag.\nL189: SIMA 2 interprets abstract concepts and logical commands by reasoning about its environment and the user's intent.\nL190: \nL191: cite50†Image cite51†Image L192: \nL193: Your browser does not support the video tag. Your browser does not support the video tag.\nL194: \nL195: SIMA 2 interprets abstract concepts and logical commands by reasoning about its environment and the user's intent.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTeaching AI to See the World More Like Humans Do — Google DeepMind (https://deepmind.google/blog/teaching-ai-to-see-the-world-more-like-we-do/)\nciteturn1952view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn1940view2\",\"id\":43}); Total lines: 199\n"
